d": "toolu_01XtHjHt5EqQ35Lu4XmFhqTY", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51794, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XtHjHt5EqQ35Lu4XmFhqTY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 53904, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. The list showed INC-0001 with the full summary, so no duplicate was created.\n\nFollow-up needed: find the cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures and of the orchestrator partial failure. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until that is fixed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RdPKqsab5WoxJvh9pSEfJb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QPY8r2hWnoHRbAH11mVCEX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": 