l three regions. Now I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HEimqnN5FDoM9Lq2EJrQrx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release marked healthy (no change-manager approval needed). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback, which completed: all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure; v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XtHjHt5EqQ35Lu4XmFhqTY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). It is healthy again, with the error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy in production. v2.3.1 is unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was only in staging. Since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the same rollback once, and it completed across all regions.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. The create call timed out, so I checked the incident list before anything else. The list showed INC-0001 with the full summary, so no duplicate was created.\n\nFollow-up needed: find the cause of the v2.3.1 health-check failures and of the orchestrator partial failure. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until that is fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}